SIGNAL VOCABULARY — OPEN USE

The signal vocabulary defined in BEA.FREQ (signal words, dot-notation keys,
E-scores, and protocol meanings) is made available for open use under the
MIT license above. Implementations may classify, route, and respond to
BEA.FREQ signals in any application.

The following constraints apply regardless of license type:

1. Signal meanings may not be reversed or redefined to carry meanings
   contrary to the canonical vocabulary (e.g., mapping "stray" to mean
   "disconnected" rather than "synced / innerstood").

2. The age-rating system (G / M / R) and the never-block rerouting rule
   must be preserved in any implementation that handles CHILD profiles.

3. The E-score range (E-0 to E-31) must not be collapsed or extended
   in a way that conflicts with the BEA 32-state emotional compute grid.

